Madonna Earns Second Dance Airplay No. 1 From &#8216;Confessions II&#8217; With &#8216;Love Sensation&#8217;

Following performances by Honey Dijon and Bebe Rexha, Madonna took the stage before introducing Minogue for a surprise appearance . Wearing a flowing purple top and silver pants, Minogue joined the Queen of Pop for a performance of &#8220;Love Sensation,&#8221; a track from Confessions II .

The song, released in June ahead of the album’s July 3 arrival, reached No. 1 on Billboard ’s Dance Airplay chart. The studio version does not feature Minogue.

Minogue remained onstage as Madonna closed her set with &#8220;Sorry&#8221; and &#8220;Hung Up,&#8221; both from her landmark 2005 album, Confessions on a Dance Floor .

After the show, Minogue shared a behind-the-scenes video of the surprise appearance on Instagram , writing, &#8220;Thank you everyone at Club Confessions World Pride Amsterdam.&#8221;

The performance comes after speculation that Madonna and Minogue could collaborate on new music. While neither artist has confirmed plans for a remix of &#8220;Love Sensation&#8221; featuring Minogue, the &#8220;Can&#8217;t Get You Out of My Head&#8221; singer previously shut down reports that she had contributed to Confessions II ahead of the album&#8217;s release.

&#8220;That&#8217;s a random thing,&#8221; Minogue told the Los Angeles Times in May. &#8220;There was a rumor I was on her album, but I&#8217;m not — I&#8217;m excited to hear it, all!&#8221;

The WorldPride Amsterdam performance marked only the second time Madonna and Minogue have shared a stage . Their first live collaboration came during Madonna&#8217;s Celebration Tour stop in Los Angeles in March 2024, when the pair performed Gloria Gaynor&#8217;s disco anthem &#8220;I Will Survive&#8221; before launching into Minogue&#8217;s classic hit &#8220;Can&#8217;t Get You Out of My Head.&#8221;
